<control>{"schema":"stage-control-v1","digest":"Keep the conditional cancellation-classification defect; read rejection still fails closed and does not demonstrate continued dispatch.","findingId":"finding-004","finding":"A rejected persistence read bypasses the post-read launch fence","verdict":"KEEP","evidence":[{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":93,"lineEnd":98,"symbol":"throwIfWorkflowStopRequested","quote":"\tif (launchStopRequested(cwd, runId))\n\t\tthrow createWorkflowStopRequestedError(runId);\n\tconst intent = await readWorkflowStopIntent(cwd, runId);\n\t// Cancellation may have arrived while the disk read was in flight.\n\tif (intent || launchStopRequested(cwd, runId))\n\t\tthrow createWorkflowStopRequestedError(runId);"},{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":53,"lineEnd":59,"symbol":"isWorkflowStopRequestedError","quote":"export function isWorkflowStopRequestedError(error: unknown): boolean {\n\treturn (\n\t\terror instanceof Error &&\n\t\t(error.name === WORKFLOW_STOP_REQUESTED_ERROR_NAME ||\n\t\t\terror.message.startsWith(\"workflow stop requested\"))\n\t);\n}"},{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":24,"lineEnd":28,"symbol":"launchStopRequested","quote":"function launchStopRequested(cwd: string, runId: string): boolean {\n\treturn [...(launchSignals.get(workflowRunPath(cwd, runId)) ?? [])].some(\n\t\t(signal) => signal.aborted,\n\t);\n}"},{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":74,"lineEnd":78,"symbol":"createWorkflowStopSignal","quote":"\t\tconst intent = await readWorkflowStopIntent(cwd, runId).catch(\n\t\t\t() => undefined,\n\t\t);\n\t\tif (intent || launchStopRequested(cwd, runId))\n\t\t\tcontroller.abort(createWorkflowStopRequestedError(runId));"}],"counterEvidence":["The rejected await still rejects the guard: this demonstrates incorrect cancellation classification, not successful dispatch past cancellation.","The polling helper catches read rejection before its second launch check, so this specific rejection race does not affect that helper."],"recommendedAction":"Catch intent-read rejection, recheck the launch fence, and throw WorkflowStopRequested only when locally stopped; otherwise rethrow the original error. Add regression tests for both outcomes."}</control>

<analysis>The proposed conditional behavior survives verification. With an un-aborted signal bound, the initial check passes. If that signal aborts while the intent read is pending and remains registered, a subsequent read rejection exits at line 95 without evaluating line 97. An ordinary persistence error then fails the stop-error classifier.

The strongest objection is that this remains fail-closed: the guard rejects rather than authorizing dispatch. The finding should therefore remain limited to cancellation classification, as its original evidence states. No downstream failed-versus-interrupted status transition is established.

The proposed correction preserves operational failures when no local stop exists and gives cancellation precedence when the registered launch signal has aborted. It need not indiscriminately swallow storage errors.

